<FictionBook xmlns="http://www.gribuser.ru/xml/fictionbook/2.0" xmlns:l="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><description><title-info><genre>unrecognised</genre><author><first-name>Test</first-name><last-name>Author</last-name></author><book-title>Fixture Book</book-title></title-info><document-info><program-used>pandoc</program-used></document-info></description><body><title><p>Fixture Book</p></title><section id="chapter-one"><title><p>Chapter One</p></title><p>It was a bright cold day in April, and the clocks were striking thirteen.</p><image l:href="#image1" l:type="imageType" alt="A small illustration" /><p>The hallway smelt of boiled cabbage and old rag mats. At one end of it a coloured poster had been tacked to the wall.</p></section><section id="chapter-two"><title><p>Chapter Two</p></title><p>The second chapter begins here with a sentence that is long enough to wrap.</p><p>A final paragraph closes the book.</p></section></body><binary id="image1" content-type="image/png"></binary></FictionBook>
